FREE USE PENDING 100,000-PERSON REVIEW

1. FREE USE PENDING REVIEW

- All individual ideas in this repository may be used freely by anyone, for any purpose, without mentioning this project, this repository, or its owner.
- Anyone may copy, rename, rewrite, combine, improve, adapt, or incorporate the ideas into their own systems, AI regulations, designs, or projects.
- The repository may continue to receive new ideas or updates. The owner is simply not controlling or tracking who uses the ideas.
- This free-use decision remains pending independent review.

2. 100,000-PERSON REVIEW

- The decision will be reviewed by at least 100,000 genuinely randomly selected ordinary people from countries that voluntarily join the AI Accord.
- 100,000 is the minimum number of qualified reviewers; there is no upper limit.
- Random selection happens first. Qualification uses only two objective checks: (1) general reasoning ability, including logic, problem-solving, probability and contradictions; and (2) basic AI knowledge, including how AI works, its capabilities and limitations.
- There is no separate test of the proposed economic decision or its outcomes, and no required coaching, preparation program or approved information source. People may learn independently from news or any other source.
- Tests must be publicly auditable, politically neutral, independently checked for unfair exclusion, and available without formal education credentials. No ideological screening, political-opinion test, preferred-outcome test, subjective interview or discretionary filtering is permitted.
- They will decide what happens afterward to 100% of the individual ideas and 100% of any revenue earned from their use anywhere in the world, by any company or person, whether in an AI Accord member country or not, and whether the ideas are renamed, modified, combined, or used without attribution.
- They may decide to keep the ideas free, or they may decide that their economic value should belong to a common fund governed by the randomly selected community.
- They may give that fund, the ideas, or the resulting system any name they want. There is no requirement to use the name "Garden" or mention the original project or owner.
- The Git owner keeps no personal economic share under this rule.

3. PROJECT RESPONSIBILITY

- The repository may continue as a place for technical ideas and future additions, but the owner has no obligation to maintain, support, approve, certify, govern, or track downstream uses.
- Use of any idea does not mean that the resulting implementation is official, certified, safe, correct, or endorsed.
- Third-party material remains subject to its own terms.

4. PERSONAL PRIVACY, ANONYMITY AND NON-INVOLVEMENT

- No attribution or personal involvement: The repository owner does not seek public credit. Do not use the owner's name, identity, image or personal information in connection with the ideas, derived systems, regulations or funds without the owner's explicit consent. No endorsement, representation or personal participation is implied.
- Full privacy and equal rights: The owner retains the same privacy, dignity, consent, security and other personal rights as every individual. Use of these ideas grants no permission to monitor, track, profile, investigate, disclose personal information about, or otherwise intrude upon the owner. No AI regulation, institution or system derived from these ideas may claim special authority over the owner because of their contribution.
- Condition of the owner's free-use offer: Respect for the owner's personal rights, including privacy, consent, dignity and security, is an express condition of the owner's offer to use the ideas for free. Anyone who unlawfully surveils, tracks or intrudes on the owner is, under the owner's stated terms, violating that condition and must stop the intrusion to restore compliance. Where monitoring is lawfully and voluntarily authorized by the owner, its scope and revocation controls must remain under the owner's informed consent. This clause does not presume surveillance is occurring or grant any new surveillance authority.
- Independent use and economic arrangements: Others may use the ideas without naming or involving the owner, subject to the existing minimum-100,000-person review rule. Any personal payment or voluntary compensation, if separately agreed, does not create an obligation to participate, provide access to private information or surrender personal rights.

Principle: Use the ideas. Leave the individual alone. No personal credit is required, and no personal rights are surrendered.

SUMMARY

The individual ideas are free to use without attribution while the review is pending. When the minimum-100,000-person review happens, the qualified randomly selected people decide what happens afterward to 100% of the ideas and all revenue earned from their use worldwide, regardless of country, company, or branding. The name "Garden" is irrelevant to that decision.
